# Owner verifies the browser

The owner checks localhost. The agent does not.

- Do not open `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, or the local Next port in the browser tools, computer-use, curl, fetch, or any other client.
- Do not start a second `next dev` (or any local server) just to self-test the UI.
- Do not screenshot, snapshot, or click the running app.
- After a UI change, say what changed and that the owner should verify. Stop there.

How it works stays in the header. That is enough for the owner to open `/how-it-works`.
